cic_api_events.db*
cic_api_usage.db*

# Compiled world packages are DERIVED, not source. records/ is the source of
# truth; `python -m engine.m2.cli build <world>` regenerates a package
# byte-identically from it (proved by determinism-check and the staleness
# sweep). At 100+ worlds (spec M1) these do not belong in a git tree -
# principle 16 puts them in S3-compatible object storage.
#
# The one exception is each package's manifest.json: 24 KB, lists every file
# with its sha256, and is the whole contract worlds.yaml pins to. It stays,
# so a clean checkout can still VERIFY a package it did not build.
packages/*/*/**
!packages/*/*/manifest.json
